  visualizations:
  - id: Viz_1
    viz_guid: 8994daac-9f94-4104-af1d-74d3cafe0f21
    note_tile:
      html_parsed_string: |-
        Key Drivers:
        • Sean Miller leads with $25,043 in sales, 32% higher than second-ranked customer
        • Top 3 customers (Miller, Chand, Buch) drive disproportionate revenue concentration
        • Sales drop significantly after top 3, with remaining customers clustered $12K-$14.6K
        • Clear tiered customer structure indicates concentrated high-value relationships

        Recommendations:
        • Develop VIP retention program for top 3 customers to protect concentrated revenue
        • Analyze purchase patterns of top performers to replicate with mid-tier customers
        • Create upselling strategy for $12K-$14K segment to move them into higher tiers
